# Container vulnerability scan exceptions.
#
# Native trivy ignore format, one entry per line:
#
#   CVE-YYYY-#### exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# The comment block directly above an entry records the remediation owner
# and the justification (see docs/image-scanning.md):
#
#   # patched in the next upstream base image digest
#   # owner:@alice
#   CVE-2025-12345 exp:2026-08-01
#
# Rules: only IDs reported by the scan may be listed, each ID at most once,
# and exp must be a valid date at most 90 days out. An expired exception
# stops being ignored and fails the daily scan again.

# CVE-2026-53615: util-linux libblkid overflow. Fixed by
# 2.41.5-0+deb13u1 in trixie-security; no python:3.14-slim digest
# ships it yet (checked 2026-08-18). Renovate bumps the digest when
# upstream rebuilds; drop this entry then.
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen
CVE-2026-53615 exp:2026-11-15

# CVE-2026-53612/53613/53614: util-linux mount TOCTOU and nosuid/noexec
# bypass. Fixed by 2.41.5-0+deb13u1 in trixie-security; no
# python:3.14-slim digest ships it yet (checked 2026-08-21). Renovate
# bumps the digest when upstream rebuilds; drop these entries then.
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen
CVE-2026-53612 exp:2026-11-15
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — TOCTOU ancestor directory swap, same fix
CVE-2026-53613 exp:2026-11-15
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — SUID mount nosuid/noexec bypass, same fix
CVE-2026-53614 exp:2026-11-15

# CVE-2026-14456: OpenSSL DoS via unbounded memory growth in QUIC server
# handling (libssl3t64). Fixed by 3.5.7-1~deb13u2 in trixie-security; no
# python:3.14-slim digest ships it yet (checked 2026-08-26). Already
# remediated in images/dbt/Dockerfile and images/superset/base/Dockerfile
# via their apt-get upgrade step; images/dagster/base/Dockerfile
# deliberately omits apt-get to keep its runtime minimal/immutable (see
# tests/test_dagster_hardening.py), so it waits on the Renovate-driven
# base image digest bump instead. SLA target per issue #526: 2026-08-29;
# revisit sooner if no digest bump has landed by then.
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen
CVE-2026-14456 exp:2026-11-15

# CVE-2026-76642/78408/78409/78410: util-linux (libuuid) HIGH findings on
# the python:3.14-alpine base used by images/dagster/hardened/Dockerfile.
# Fixed by util-linux 2.42.3-r0; the pinned python:3.14-alpine digest
# still ships libuuid-2.42.1-r0 and no newer digest has been published
# upstream yet (checked 2026-09-05, same digest as `docker pull
# python:3.14-alpine` resolves to today). Renovate bumps the digest when
# upstream rebuilds; drop these entries then.
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — mount post-hook privileged X-mount.idmap/owner escalation
CVE-2026-76642 exp:2026-12-04
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — nsenter --join-cgroup root cgroup migration leak, same fix
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2026-12-04
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — X-mount.subdir detached-tree symlink escape, same fix
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2026-12-04
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — restricted bind mount owner/group/mode pin bypass, same fix
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-12-04

# CVE-2026-41992/86145/89161/11822/11824/13221/42496/8376/42497/48962/57432/57433:
# gzip, libpcre2-8-0, libsqlite3-0, and perl-base HIGH/CRITICAL findings on the
# python:3.14-slim base used by images/dagster/base/Dockerfile. All are fixed by
# trixie-security package versions (gzip 1.13-1+deb13u1, libpcre2-8-0
# 10.46-1~deb13u2, libsqlite3-0 3.46.1-7+deb13u2, perl-base 5.40.1-6+deb13u1);
# no python:3.14-slim digest ships them yet (checked 2026-09-12, same digest as
# `docker pull python:3.14-slim` resolves to today). Already remediated in
# images/dbt/Dockerfile and images/superset/base/Dockerfile via their apt-get
# upgrade step; images/dagster/base/Dockerfile deliberately omits apt-get to
# keep its runtime minimal/immutable (see tests/test_dagster_hardening.py), so
# it waits on the Renovate-driven base image digest bump instead. Renovate
# bumps the digest when upstream rebuilds; drop these entries then.
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — gzip: information disclosure via global buffer overflow in LZH decompression
CVE-2026-41992 exp:2026-12-01
# owner:@RonaldHensbergen — libpcre2-8-0: out-of-bounds write via crafted regular expressions, same fix
CVE-2026-86145 exp:2026-12-01
